Tokenization of various Assets

ASSET TOKENIZATION: 
Tokenization of assets is the process of converting ownership rights of a physical or financial asset into digital tokens recorded on a blockchain.

How It Works:
Digital Representation: An asset is linked to a unique cryptographic token on a distributed ledger or blockchain. 
Smart Contracts: Self-executing code automates rules, transfers, and compliance conditions without traditional middlemen.
Fungible or Non-Fungible: Tokens can be interchangeable (fungible, like shares or currency) or unique (non-fungible tokens or NFTs, like rare art).

Common Examples:
Real Estate: Commercial or residential buildings split into digital shares.
Financial Instruments: Government bonds, stocks, and private funds.
Commodities: Precious metals like gold or barrels of oil.Currency: Fiat-backed stablecoins representing cash.

Key Benefits:
Fractional Ownership: Assets are easily divided, allowing smaller investors to buy a fraction of high-value items like real estate.
Increased Liquidity: Digital tokens trade faster and easier on digital markets.
Transparency & Speed: Settlements happen almost instantly with a clear, immutable audit trail on the blockchain.
